msgid "Configuration reference"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides two configuration properties to control native transport behavior.\n"
"Both are **build-time properties** (fixed at build time), meaning they are resolved during the Quarkus augmentation phase.\n"
"They can be set in `application.properties` and overridden using Quarkus profiles (e.g., `%dev`, `%prod`), but cannot be changed at runtime via environment variables."
msgstr ""

msgid "Property"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default"
msgstr "Padrão"

msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descrição"

msgid "`quarkus.vertx.native-transport` icon:lock[title=Fixed at build time]"
msgstr ""

msgid "`disabled`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Controls whether and how strictly native transport should be used. Accepted values: `disabled` (do not use native transport), `if-available` (use native transport if available, fall back to Java NIO otherwise), `required` (require native transport, the build fails if the dependency is missing, the application fails to start if the native library cannot load)."
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.vertx.native-transport-type` icon:lock[title=Fixed at build time]"
msgstr ""

msgid "`auto`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Select a specific transport: `auto` (let Vert.x choose), `epoll`, `kqueue`, or `io-uring`. Setting this to a value other than `auto` implicitly enables native transport (treated as at least `if-available`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Property relationships"
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting `native-transport=disabled` disables native transport entirely."
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting `native-transport-type` to a specific value (e.g., `epoll`) implicitly enables native transport, even if `native-transport` is `disabled`."
msgstr ""

msgid "When `native-transport=required`, missing dependencies cause a build failure, and a transport that cannot load at runtime causes a startup failure."
msgstr ""

msgid "Example configurations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Profile-based configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Since native transport properties are fixed at build time, you can use Quarkus profiles to configure different transports per environment.\n"
"This is useful when developing on macOS and deploying on Linux:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `%dev` profile applies during `quarkus dev`, while `%prod` applies when building production artifacts.\n"
"This lets you develop locally without native transport dependencies and enforce them in production."
msgstr ""

msgid "Build-time and runtime checks"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus performs two-stage validation of native transport configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Build-time validation"
msgstr ""

msgid "During the build, Quarkus scans the classpath for native transport dependencies and validates them against the configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "If `native-transport-type` is set to a specific transport (e.g., `epoll`) but the corresponding dependency is missing:"
msgstr ""

msgid "When `native-transport=required`: the build **fails** with a `ConfigurationException`."
msgstr ""

msgid "When `native-transport=if-available`: the build logs a warning and continues. The application will fall back to Java NIO at runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid "If `native-transport=if-available` but no native transport dependency is found, the build logs a warning."
msgstr ""

msgid "Runtime behavior"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Even when a transport dependency is on the classpath, the native library may fail to load at runtime (e.g., running on a different platform, or the kernel does not support io_uring).\n"
"Quarkus checks the actual transport status at startup:"
msgstr ""

msgid "When <code>native-transport=if-available</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid "If the transport fails to load, Quarkus logs a warning and falls back to Java NIO."
msgstr ""

msgid "When <code>native-transport=required</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid "If the transport fails to load, the application fails to start with an `IllegalStateException`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Transport type mismatch"
msgstr ""

msgid "If you request a specific transport type (e.g., `epoll`) but a different transport loaded (e.g., `io_uring`), the application logs a warning or fails depending on the `native-transport` setting."
msgstr ""

msgid "Platform-specific socket options"
msgstr ""

msgid "Native transports provide access to platform-specific socket options not available with Java NIO."
msgstr ""

msgid "Linux (epoll and io_uring)"
msgstr ""

msgid "SO_REUSEPORT"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Allows multiple sockets to bind to the same address and port.\n"
"The kernel distributes incoming connections across the sockets, improving scalability."
msgstr ""

msgid "TCP_QUICKACK"
msgstr ""

msgid "Disables delayed ACKs, reducing latency for request-response protocols."
msgstr ""

msgid "TCP_CORK"
msgstr ""

msgid "Buffers small packets until the buffer is full or the cork is removed, reducing the number of packets sent."
msgstr ""

msgid "TCP_FASTOPEN"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enables TCP Fast Open, allowing data to be sent in the SYN packet during connection establishment."
msgstr ""

msgid "TCP_USER_TIMEOUT"
msgstr ""

msgid "Sets the maximum time (in milliseconds) that transmitted data may remain unacknowledged before the connection is forcibly closed."
msgstr ""

msgid "OSX (kqueue)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Same functionality as Linux (see above)."
msgstr ""

msgid "epoll vs io_uring"
msgstr ""

msgid "Both epoll and io_uring are available on Linux. Which should you use?"
msgstr ""

